sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as odh-dashboard<br/>(BFF sidecars)
    participant KF as kubeflow<br/>(notebook-controller)
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>(sidecar)
    participant KServe as kserve<br/>(manager)
    participant ODHMC as odh-model-controller
    participant DSG as data-science-gateway<br/>(Istio/Envoy)
    participant KAP as kube-auth-proxy
    participant NB as Notebook Server<br/>(JupyterLab)
    participant IS as InferenceService<br/>(vLLM/MLServer)
    participant S3 as Object Storage<br/>(S3)
    participant Client as External Client

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 1: Model Deployment via KServe InferenceService

    User->>Dashboard: Login via OAuth2/OIDC
    Dashboard-->>User: Show dashboard UI (11 BFF sidecars)
    User->>Dashboard: Create InferenceService via UI
    Dashboard->>KServe: Create InferenceService CR<br/>(Kubernetes API, SA token)

    KServe->>KServe: Validate via webhook (30 webhooks)<br/>Reconcile ServingRuntime pod,<br/>Service, model server container
    KServe->>ODHMC: InferenceService created event

    ODHMC->>DSG: Create HTTPRoute targeting<br/>data-science-gateway
    ODHMC->>ODHMC: Create Kuadrant AuthPolicy<br/>Create EnvoyFilter/DestinationRule

    Note over DSG: Gateway ready for inference traffic

    Client->>DSG: POST /v1/models/my-model:predict<br/>(HTTPS/443, TLS)
    DSG->>KAP: ext_authz subrequest to<br/>/oauth2/auth (port 8443)
    KAP-->>DSG: 202 Accepted + identity headers<br/>(x-auth-request-user,<br/>x-auth-request-access-token)
    DSG->>IS: Forward to model server<br/>(Lua filter strips OAuth cookies)
    IS->>S3: Download model artifacts<br/>(AWS IAM / S3 credentials)
    IS-->>DSG: Inference result
    DSG-->>Client: JSON response (HTTPS/443)

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 2: MaaS External Model Inference

    participant MaaS_GW as maas-default-gateway<br/>(Istio/Envoy)
    participant Praxis as praxis-extproc<br/>(dual-stage)
    participant Authorino as Kuadrant/Authorino
    participant MaaS_API as maas-api
    participant ExtProvider as External Model<br/>Provider

    Client->>MaaS_GW: POST /v1/models<br/>(API key sk-oai-* or<br/>OpenShift bearer token)
    MaaS_GW->>Praxis: ipp-pre (pre-auth, fail-open)<br/>Extract model identifier
    Praxis-->>MaaS_GW: Model routing metadata
    MaaS_GW->>Authorino: Kuadrant WasmPlugin auth<br/>Validate API key or token
    Authorino-->>MaaS_GW: Auth result + metadata
    MaaS_GW->>Praxis: ipp (post-auth, fail-closed)<br/>Full payload processing pipeline
    Praxis-->>MaaS_GW: Processed request
    MaaS_GW->>MaaS_API: Forward to maas-api (port 8443)
    MaaS_API->>MaaS_API: Resolve subscription, tenant,<br/>model configuration
    MaaS_API->>ExtProvider: Proxy to external provider<br/>(OpenAI-compatible API, TLS)
    ExtProvider-->>MaaS_API: Inference result
    MaaS_API-->>MaaS_GW: Response
    MaaS_GW-->>Client: JSON response (HTTPS/443)

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 3: Notebook Creation and Access

    User->>Dashboard: Request new Notebook via UI
    Dashboard->>KF: Create Notebook CR<br/>(Kubernetes API, SA token)
    KF->>KF: Reconcile Notebook CR<br/>Create StatefulSet, Service
    KF->>KF: Mutating webhook injects<br/>kube-rbac-proxy sidecar
    KF->>DSG: Create HTTPRoute targeting<br/>data-science-gateway<br/>(with ReferenceGrant for<br/>cross-namespace access)
    KF->>KF: Create NetworkPolicy for<br/>notebook isolation

    User->>DSG: Access notebook URL<br/>(HTTPS/443)
    DSG->>KAP: ext_authz → /oauth2/auth
    KAP-->>DSG: 202 Accepted + identity headers
    DSG->>KRBP: Forward to kube-rbac-proxy sidecar
    KRBP->>KRBP: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>(per-user authorization)
    KRBP->>NB: Forward to notebook server
    NB-->>KRBP: JupyterLab response
    KRBP-->>DSG: Response
    DSG-->>User: Notebook UI (HTTPS)

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 4: Data Science Pipeline Execution

    participant DSPO as data-science-pipelines-operator
    participant DSP_API as DSP API Server
    participant Argo as Argo Workflows
    participant MariaDB as MariaDB
    participant MLMD as ml-metadata

    User->>Dashboard: Submit pipeline run via UI
    Dashboard->>DSPO: Create pipeline run<br/>(Kubernetes API)
    DSPO->>DSPO: Reconcile DataSciencePipelinesApplication<br/>Deploy API server (8888/8887),<br/>Argo controller, MariaDB, MinIO
    DSPO->>DSP_API: Pipeline submission
    DSP_API->>MariaDB: Store pipeline metadata
    DSP_API->>Argo: Create Argo Workflow CR
    Argo->>Argo: Orchestrate pipeline steps<br/>as Kubernetes pods
    Argo->>S3: Read/write pipeline artifacts
    Argo->>MLMD: Record artifacts, executions,<br/>lineage (gRPC via metadata-envoy)
    MLMD-->>DSP_API: Lineage data
    DSP_API-->>Dashboard: Pipeline status
    Dashboard-->>User: Pipeline results

    Note over User,Client: Workflow 5: LLM-D Disaggregated Inference

    participant Envoy as Envoy Proxy<br/>(port 8081)
    participant EPP as llm-d-router (EPP)<br/>(ExtProc, port 9002)
    participant vLLM_P as vLLM Prefill Node
    participant KVCache as llm-d-kv-cache<br/>(RDMA port 5600)
    participant vLLM_D as vLLM Decode Node

    Client->>Envoy: Inference request (port 8081)
    Envoy->>EPP: ExtProc gRPC call (port 9002)<br/>Plugin-based scheduling pipeline
    EPP->>EPP: Select optimal backend via<br/>InferencePool abstraction
    EPP-->>Envoy: Set x-gateway-destination-endpoint<br/>header for routing
    Envoy->>vLLM_P: Route to prefill node
    vLLM_P->>vLLM_P: Compute prefill (KV-cache)
    vLLM_P->>KVCache: Transfer KV-cache via<br/>RDMA (port 5600)
    KVCache->>vLLM_D: Deliver KV-cache to<br/>decode node
    vLLM_D->>vLLM_D: Generate tokens<br/>(decode phase)
    vLLM_D-->>Envoy: Inference result
    Envoy-->>Client: Response
